+| `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` | Stripe API secret key |
+| `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | Signing secret for this webhook endpoint |
+| `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID` | Recurring USD $20/month price for Unlimited |
+| `STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID` | Recurring USD $25/month price for Unlimited+ (the full price, not an add-on) |
 
-Then, for working on the Stripe integration locally, you need to run this script to start the tunneling and set the environment variables:
+Configure Checkout and the Stripe customer portal for those two recurring prices. In the portal, enable switching between the prices, updating payment details, and canceling subscriptions. Configure Stripe to send `customer.subscription.created`, `.updated`, `.deleted`, `.paused`, and `.resumed` events to `POST /stripe/webhooks`. Signed events for known customers trigger a refresh from Stripe, so duplicate or out-of-order deliveries don't undo a newer change. Active and trialing subscriptions receive the corresponding plan limits.
 
